# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Library & Resource Management API: a runnable demo
#
# How to use:
#   • VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
#     then click "Send Request" above any request.
#   • Visual Studio 2022 (17.12+): open this file and click the green ▶ next to a request.
#   • Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/LibraryManagement.Api --launch-profile http
#
# Send the four LOGIN requests (section 1) first. Every other request reads the
# token straight from those responses, so you never copy and paste a JWT.
#
# Section 4 changes the sample data. To reset it:
#   dotnet ef database drop -f --project src/LibraryManagement.Api   (then restart the app)
# Fines grow daily: the ₹ amounts below are true on the day the database was seeded.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@api = http://localhost:5180/api


###
# ═══ 1. LOGIN ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# @name admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@library.local", "password": "Admin@123" }

###
# @name alice
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Member@123" }

###
# @name bob
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "Member@123" }

###
# @name carol
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "carol@example.com", "password": "Member@123" }


###
# ═══ 2. CATALOGUE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Search by category (partial, case-insensitive)  → 3 fiction books
GET {{api}}/books?category=fiction
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

###
# Search by author  → Wings of Fire
GET {{api}}/books?author=kalam
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

###
# Librarian adds a book (hyphens in the ISBN are stripped)  → 201
# @name newBook
POST {{api}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Refactoring", "author": "Martin Fowler", "isbn": "978-0-13-475759-9", "category": "Software", "totalCopies": 2 }

###
# Librarian deletes it again  → 204
DELETE {{api}}/books/{{newBook.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

###
# A member can't add books  → 403
POST {{api}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Nope", "author": "Nobody", "isbn": "9780000000002", "category": "X", "totalCopies": 1 }


###
# ═══ 3. REPORTS (librarian only) ════════════════════════════════════════════
# Top 5 most borrowed  → Clean Code (6), Atomic Habits (4), ...
GET {{api}}/reports/most-borrowed
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

###
# Overdue loans with fines owed  → 2 loans, ₹110 total (on the day of seeding)
GET {{api}}/reports/overdue-loans
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}


###
# ═══ 4. THE RESERVATION QUEUE (send in order) ═══════════════════════════════
# "The God of Small Things" (book 5) has 1 copy. Bob has it, 16 days overdue.
# Carol reserved it first, Alice second.
#
# 4a. The queue  → Carol #1, Alice #2 (both Pending)
GET {{api}}/reservations/book/5
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

###
# 4b. Carol tries to borrow  → 409 "No copies available. Reserve it instead"
POST {{api}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 5 }

###
# 4c. Bob's active loans (his only loan is book 5)
# @name bobLoans
GET {{api}}/loans/active
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}

###
# 4d. Bob returns it  → fineAmount ₹80 (16 days × ₹5). Carol is notified (see the app log).
POST {{api}}/loans/{{bobLoans.response.body.$[0].id}}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}

###
# 4e. The queue again  → Carol is Notified (the copy is held for her), Alice still Pending
GET {{api}}/reservations/book/5
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

###
# 4f. Alice tries to take the held copy  → 409
POST {{api}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 5 }

###
# 4g. Carol borrows her held copy  → 201, due in 14 days
POST {{api}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 5 }

###
# 4h. Alice's reservations  → she is now Pending, queuePosition 1
GET {{api}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}


###
# ═══ 5. ERROR HANDLING (all return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails) ═════════════════
# Validation errors, field by field  → 400
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "A", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short" }

###
# Wrong password  → 401
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Wrong123" }

###
# No token  → 401
GET {{api}}/books

###
# A member looking at another member's loans  → 403
GET {{api}}/loans/active?memberId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

###
# Reserving a book that has free copies  → 409 "Borrow it instead"
POST {{api}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 7 }
